{"title":"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The squares shown are each filled with a number so that the sum of the numbers in every group of three consecutive squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What number appears in the square marked with a question mark?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc346911ad0c6b9edd274cd861435a94191d81cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the sum of the numbers for every group of three consecutive numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the fourth number must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72f9c083cc550ecdfe8ee34510baeaad5b33dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 - (5 + 16) = 24 - 21 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The fifth number must then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8ae955f8caf66f6c3f3b9981004165fa2672acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 - (3 + 16) = 24 - 19 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The sixth number would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc446c7ca2f0cb9d83322de7ee96589b9910dd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 - (5 + 3) = 24 - 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The last number would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddcba356b290f1eece807bec1ce377cff82510dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 - (5 + 16) = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"186\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Pattern.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Pattern)\">Solution 2 (Using Pattern)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Pattern)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Due to the group of three consecutive rule, we can realize that the numbers would have to repeat every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705f8d7397c6efd511be220d8b8fa2241c4190d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c67f8655a7b6f77ee5a4b82e9cae797bc2895e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 + x_3 + x_4 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/85004cd9287a564fecc39a9d323b8bea82ea70f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = x_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f831fb27980f11f3f96781e82f8b8be320d162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th number would be the same as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />st number, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874eca3c2b98beae5bebd0dfc4ba2205eb666c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat\">2026 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_17&amp